# T-1890: Dot-access on a concrete dict produces precise field types.
# n@String: person.name — the annotation is checked at runtime by TypeAssert;
# the precise StringLiteral("Alice") type is a subtype of String, so it passes.
# a@Integer: person.age — Int(30) is a subtype of Integer, so it also passes.
[
  person: [name: "Alice"  age: 30]
  n@String: person.name
  a@Integer: person.age
]
=== out
Dict({"person": Dict({"name": String("Alice"), "age": Int(30)}), "n": String("Alice"), "a": Int(30)})
